  "fact_notes": [
    "人物・出来事・制度は架空の教材例。実在の調査・統計・実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A fictional bakery became popular after introducing a subscription service that allowed customers to reserve bread in advance.",
          "ja": "架空のパン店は事前予約できる定期購入サービスで人気になった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "When demand exceeded its capacity, an investor proposed opening several additional branches in nearby towns.",
          "ja": "需要が供給能力を超えると投資家は近隣に支店を増やす案を出した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The owner recognized the potential revenue but questioned whether expansion would preserve the conditions that had made the original service attractive.",
          "ja": "収益の可能性は認めたが拡大で元のサービスの魅力を支える条件を保てるか疑問に思った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Her hesitation surprised employees who had interpreted increasing sales as the clearest indication of business success.",
          "ja": "売上増を成功の最も明確な指標と考えていた従業員は驚いた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The owner examined the resources required for the proposed expansion rather than comparing anticipated sales alone.",
          "ja": "予想売上だけでなく拡大に必要な資源を調べた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Each branch would require trained staff, reliable suppliers and a procedure for maintaining consistent quality across different locations.",
          "ja": "各支店には訓練した職員、信頼できる供給業者、一定品質を保つ手順が必要だった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Moreover, coordinating production might increase administrative work that was not reflected in the original financial projection.",
          "ja": "さらに製造調整で当初の財務予測に反映されない事務作業が増える可能性があった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She therefore asked whether the projected increase in revenue would compensate for the additional obligations.",
          "ja": "予想収益増が追加の義務を補えるか尋ねた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Instead of rejecting expansion entirely, the bakery tested a limited partnership with an independent shop.",
          "ja": "拡大を完全に拒まず独立店舗との限定的な提携を試した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The partner distributed a fixed quantity of products while the bakery retained responsibility for production.",
          "ja": "提携先は一定量の商品を販売しパン店は製造責任を維持した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The trial made it possible to observe whether customers valued accessibility or the direct relationship with the original shop.",
          "ja": "顧客が利用のしやすさと元の店との直接関係のどちらを重視するか観察できた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The agreement included a review date so that neither business had to regard the experiment as a permanent commitment.",
          "ja": "見直し日を合意に含め、恒久的な約束と見なす必要をなくした。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Some customers appreciated the convenient location, while others continued visiting the bakery despite having a closer alternative.",
          "ja": "便利な場所を評価する顧客もいれば、近い選択肢があっても元の店を訪れる人もいた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The results suggested that demand was not necessarily identical across distribution channels.",
          "ja": "結果は流通経路によって需要が必ずしも同じでないことを示唆した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The owner acknowledged that the brief trial could not establish the profitability of a larger network.",
          "ja": "短い試行ではより大きなネットワークの収益性は確定できないと認めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Nevertheless, it clarified which assumptions would require investigation before a substantial investment could be justified.",
          "ja": "それでも大きな投資を正当化する前に検討すべき前提が明確になった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Business growth is sometimes discussed as though greater scale were an objective that required no further explanation.",
          "ja": "事業成長は規模拡大が説明不要の目標であるかのように語られることがある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Yet a decision to expand should distinguish the financial benefits from the operational risks and competing priorities.",
          "ja": "しかし拡大判断では金銭的利益と運営上のリスク、競合する優先事項を区別すべきだ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A sustainable enterprise may choose to increase its reach gradually while protecting the features that customers actually value.",
          "ja": "持続可能な企業は顧客が実際に重視する特徴を守りつつ徐々に範囲を広げるかもしれない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The bakery's decision was not a rejection of ambition but an attempt to define what worthwhile growth would mean.",
          "ja": "店の判断は野心の拒絶でなく価値ある成長の意味を定義する試みだった。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
